From: rdndds <rdndds@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 09:16:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] NetBpfLoad: do not abort on absent bpf_jit sysctls

The bpf_jit_enable and bpf_jit_kallsyms writes are guarded by
isAtLeastKernelVersion(4, 14, 0), which is true on this device's 4.14.186
kernel. Both sysctls are absent when the kernel is built with
CONFIG_BPF_JIT_ALWAYS_ON=y, which is how this kernel is built, so
writeProcSysFile() returns true and the process exits 1.

bpfloader is a oneshot service declared with
"reboot_on_failure reboot,bpfloader-failed", so that exit reboots the
device before the framework starts.

Raise the guard to 5.4. JIT is already forced on by the kernel config, and
the kallsyms export is only a debugging aid.

The 4.14 branch of this code predates the assumption that the sysctls are
writable; only 5.4+ kernels have a writable bpf_jit_enable when JIT is
forced on.

Signed-off-by: rdndds <rdndds@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp b/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp
index 48ca600..04b8818 100644
--- a/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp
+++ b/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp
@@ -1599,13 +1599,13 @@ static int doLoad(char** argv, char * const envp[]) {
         // BPF_JIT is required by R VINTF (which means 4.14/4.19/5.4 kernels),
         // but 4.14/4.19 were released with P & Q, and only 5.4 is new in R+.
         if (writeProcSysFile("/proc/sys/net/core/bpf_jit_enable", "1\n") &&
-            android::bpf::isAtLeastKernelVersion(4, 14, 0)) return 1;
+            android::bpf::isAtLeastKernelVersion(5, 4, 0)) return 1;
 
         // Enable JIT kallsyms export for privileged users only
         // (Note: this (open) will fail with ENOENT 'No such file or directory' if
         //  kernel does not have CONFIG_HAVE_EBPF_JIT=y)
         if (writeProcSysFile("/proc/sys/net/core/bpf_jit_kallsyms", "1\n") &&
-            android::bpf::isAtLeastKernelVersion(4, 14, 0)) return 1;
+            android::bpf::isAtLeastKernelVersion(5, 4, 0)) return 1;
     }
 
     // Create all the pin subdirectories
